"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[35266],{535266:e=>{e.exports="# Info: Silver table configuration\n\nSilver tables sit between Bronze and Gold; this skill covers field specs, joins, pre/post-filter, and addTables vs modifyTables.\n\nFor nested JSON columns: {{JSON_EXTRACT_BRANCH_GUIDANCE}}\n\n{{JSON_EXTRACT_EXAMPLE_SECTION}}\n\n## Example: Field Transformation\n\nAdd computed fields or derived values based on existing columns.\n\n**User Request:** \"Add a field 'is_admin' that's true when role contains 'admin'\"\n\n**Sample Response:**\n\n```\nI'll add a boolean field 'is_admin' that checks if the 'role' field contains 'admin'.\n\nThe SQL expression will be:\nCAST(LOWER(role) LIKE '%admin%' AS BOOLEAN)\n\nThis will return:\n- TRUE when role contains 'admin' (case-insensitive)\n- FALSE otherwise\n\nWould you like me to:\n1. Apply this change?\n2. Use a different matching logic (exact match, starts with, etc.)?\n```\n\n**Configuration Generated:**\n\n```yaml\nsilver:\n  transform:\n    presetOverrides:\n      modifyTables:\n        - name: <silver_table_name>\n          addFields:\n            - name: is_admin\n              expr: \"CAST(LOWER(role) LIKE '%admin%' AS BOOLEAN)\"\n```\n\n## Example: Filtering\n\nApply filters to include or exclude records based on conditions.\n\n**User Request:** \"Filter out internal IP addresses\"\n\n**Sample Response:**\n\n```\nI found the 'src_ip' field in your bronze table. To filter out internal IPs, I'll exclude:\n- 10.0.0.0/8 (10.x.x.x)\n- 172.16.0.0/12 (172.16-31.x.x)\n- 192.168.0.0/16 (192.168.x.x)\n\nThis will be applied as a pre-filter to exclude these IPs before any transformations.\n\nIs this correct, or do you have specific IP ranges to exclude?\n```\n\n**Configuration Generated:**\n\n```yaml\nsilver:\n  transform:\n    presetOverrides:\n      modifyTables:\n        - name: <silver_table_name>\n          filter: >\n            NOT (\n              src_ip LIKE '10.%' OR \n              src_ip LIKE '172.16.%' OR src_ip LIKE '172.17.%' OR \n              src_ip LIKE '192.168.%'\n            )\n```\n\n## Example: Joins\n\nEnrich data by joining with external tables.\n\n**User Request:** \"Join with user directory to enrich with department info\"\n\n**Sample Response:**\n\n```\nI found a potential match: 'main.users.employee_directory'\n\nThis table has:\n- Join key: 'email' (matches your 'user_email' field)\n- Available fields: department, office_location, manager_email, cost_center\n\nI'll configure a static join (streaming: false) to add:\n- department\n- office_location\n\nWould you like to:\n1. Add these fields?\n2. Include additional fields from the directory?\n3. Use a different join type?\n```\n\n**Configuration Generated:**\n\n```yaml\nsilver:\n  bronzeTables:\n    - name: <bronze_table>\n    - name: main.users.employee_directory\n      alias: emp_dir\n      streaming: false # Static join for reference data\n      joinType: left\n      lhs: 'user_email'\n      rhs: 'email'\n  transform:\n    presetOverrides:\n      modifyTables:\n        - name: <silver_table>\n          addFields:\n            - name: department\n              expr: 'emp_dir.department'\n            - name: office_location\n              expr: 'emp_dir.office_location'\n```\n\n## Example: Column Preservation\n\nControl how unreferenced columns are handled.\n\n**User Request:** \"Preserve all unreferenced columns from bronze\"\n\n**Sample Response:**\n\n```\nUnreferenced columns are fields in the bronze table that aren't explicitly mapped in your field specs (via the `from` attribute).\n\nYou have 3 options:\n1. **Preserve**: Keep them as individual columns in silver (recommended for flexibility)\n2. **Embed**: Bundle them into a single column (saves space, useful for rarely-accessed fields)\n3. **Omit**: Drop them completely (only keep explicitly defined fields)\n\nI recommend option 1 (preserve) to ensure no data loss if bronze schema changes.\n\nWhich option would you like?\n```\n\n**Configuration Generated:**\n\n```yaml\nsilver:\n  transform:\n    presetOverrides:\n      modifyTables:\n        - name: <silver_table_name>\n          utils:\n            unreferencedColumns:\n              preserve: true\n```\n\n**For embed option:**\n\n```yaml\nutils:\n  unreferencedColumns:\n    preserve: true\n    embedColumn: 'raw_bronze_data'\n    embedColumnType: 'variant' # Options: json, struct, variant\n```\n\n**Full unreferencedColumns options:**\n\n```yaml\nutils:\n  unreferencedColumns:\n    preserve: true # Keep unreferenced columns\n    embedColumn: 'raw_data' # Optional: bundle into single column\n    embedColumnType: 'variant' # Optional: json, struct, or variant\n    omitColumns: ['debug', 'internal'] # Optional: exclude specific columns\n    duplicatePrefix: 'bronze_' # Optional: prefix for name conflicts\n```\n\n## Example: Creating Derived Tables (addTables)\n\nCreate new silver tables from bronze data with custom schemas or filters.\n\n**User Request:** \"Create a new silver table for only authentication events\"\n\n**Sample Response:**\n\n```\nI'll create a new silver table derived from your bronze data.\n\nBased on the bronze schema, I found an 'event_type' field that can filter events.\n\nTo create a table for authentication events, I need:\n1. **Table name**: What should I call this table? (e.g., 'auth_events_silver')\n2. **Filter**: I'll use `event_type = 'authentication'` - is this correct?\n3. **Fields**: Do you want all bronze fields, or specific ones only?\n\nNote: This creates an entirely NEW silver table, separate from any preset-defined tables.\n```\n\n**Configuration Generated:**\n\n```yaml\nsilver:\n  transform:\n    presetOverrides:\n      addTables:\n        - name: auth_events_silver\n          filter: \"event_type = 'authentication'\"\n          utils:\n            unreferencedColumns:\n              preserve: true\n```\n\n**Example: Split bronze into multiple tables by event_type:**\n\n```yaml\nsilver:\n  transform:\n    presetOverrides:\n      addTables:\n        - name: login_events_silver\n          filter: \"event_type = 'login'\"\n        - name: logout_events_silver\n          filter: \"event_type = 'logout'\"\n        - name: password_events_silver\n          filter: \"event_type = 'password_change'\"\n```\n\n**Example: Custom schema with specific fields:**\n\n```yaml\nsilver:\n  transform:\n    presetOverrides:\n      addTables:\n        - name: threat_detection_silver\n          filter: 'severity >= 3'\n          fields:\n            - name: event_time\n              from: timestamp\n            - name: source_ip\n              from: src_ip\n            - name: is_failed\n              expr: \"status != 'success'\"\n          utils:\n            unreferencedColumns:\n              preserve: false # Only keep explicitly defined fields\n```\n\n## Key Configuration Concepts\n\n### addTables vs modifyTables\n\n| Aspect         | `addTables`                   | `modifyTables`                |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| **Purpose**    | Create NEW tables from bronze | Modify EXISTING preset tables |\n| **Schema**     | Fully user-defined            | Extends preset schema         |\n| **Table name** | Must be unique, user-chosen   | Must match preset table name  |\n| **Use case**   | Custom tables, splitting data | Customizing preset behavior   |\n\n**When to use `addTables`:**\n\n- User wants to create a table that doesn't exist in the preset\n- User wants to split bronze data into multiple tables\n- User wants a custom schema not defined by the preset\n- User says \"create\", \"add\", \"new table\", \"split into tables\"\n\n**When to use `modifyTables`:**\n\n- User wants to modify an existing preset-defined table\n- User says \"add field to\", \"modify\", \"change\", \"update\"\n\n**How to update a preset field:** (1) Add the preset field name to `omitFields` so the preset definition is not used. (2) Add a field with the same name in `addFields` with the new definition (`from`, `expr`, etc.). Do not only add to addFields without omitting—that can duplicate or conflict with the preset column.\n\n### Field Specification Types\n\n1. **from** - Copy field from bronze/previous stage:\n\n   ```yaml\n   - name: event_time\n     from: eventTime\n   ```\n\n2. **expr** - SQL expression:\n\n   ```yaml\n   - name: severity_text\n     expr: \"CASE severity WHEN 1 THEN 'Low' WHEN 2 THEN 'Medium' ELSE 'High' END\"\n   ```\n\n3. **literal** - Static value:\n\n   ```yaml\n   - name: source_system\n     literal: 'firewall'\n   ```\n\n4. **alias** - Reference another field in same stage:\n\n   ```yaml\n   - name: timestamp_copy\n     alias: event_time\n   ```\n\n5. **join** - Value from joined table (configured separately in bronzeTables)\n\n{{JSON_EXTRACT_CONFIGURATION_SECTION}}\n\n### Bronze Table Joins\n\nJoins are configured in `silver.bronzeTables`. The first entry is the main bronze table.\n\n**Simple equijoin using lhs/rhs:**\n\n```yaml\nsilver:\n  bronzeTables:\n    - name: main_bronze_table\n    - name: reference_table\n      alias: ref\n      streaming: false # false = static join, true = streaming join\n      joinType: left # left, right, inner, outer\n      lhs: 'main_column' # Column from accumulated result\n      rhs: 'ref_column' # Column from this table\n```\n\n**Complex join using joinExpr:**\n\n```yaml\nsilver:\n  bronzeTables:\n    - name: main_bronze_table\n    - name: reference_table\n      alias: ref\n      streaming: false\n      joinType: left\n      joinExpr: 'main_bronze_table.user_id = ref.id AND ref.active = true'\n```\n\n### Filtering\n\n**Pre-filter** (applied before field transformations):\n\n```yaml\nfilter: \"event_type IN ('login', 'logout') AND severity >= 3\"\n```\n\n**Post-filter** (applied after field transformations):\n\n```yaml\npostFilter: 'is_valid = true AND processed_timestamp IS NOT NULL'\n```\n\n### Temporary Fields\n\nIntermediate calculations that are NOT saved to silver table:\n\n```yaml\nutils:\n  temporaryFields:\n    - name: temp_ts\n      expr: 'CAST(time_millis / 1000 AS BIGINT)'\nfields:\n  - name: event_time\n    expr: 'FROM_UNIXTIME(temp_ts)'\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Basic Field Mapping\n\n```yaml\naddFields:\n  - name: user_id\n    from: userId\n  - name: timestamp\n    expr: 'CAST(eventTime AS TIMESTAMP)'\n  - name: event_source\n    literal: 'application_logs'\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Conditional Field\n\n```yaml\naddFields:\n  - name: is_suspicious\n    expr: \"CASE WHEN (failed_attempts > 5 OR login_time < '06:00' OR login_time > '22:00') THEN TRUE ELSE FALSE END\"\n```\n\n{{JSON_EXTRACT_PATTERN_SECTION}}\n\n### Pattern 4: Multi-Table Join with Enrichment\n\n```yaml\nsilver:\n  bronzeTables:\n    - name: security_logs_bronze\n    - name: main.reference.ip_reputation\n      alias: ip_rep\n      streaming: false\n      joinType: left\n      lhs: 'src_ip'\n      rhs: 'ip_address'\n    - name: main.reference.user_directory\n      alias: users\n      streaming: false\n      joinType: left\n      lhs: 'user_email'\n      rhs: 'email'\n  transform:\n    presetOverrides:\n      modifyTables:\n        - name: security_logs_silver\n          addFields:\n            - name: threat_score\n              expr: 'ip_rep.reputation_score'\n            - name: user_department\n              expr: 'users.department'\n```\n\n## Important Considerations\n\n1. **Required: time column** — Silver and gold tables must have a `time` column of TIMESTAMP type.\n\n2. **Data Types**: Always cast values to appropriate types (STRING, INT, TIMESTAMP, BOOLEAN, VARIANT)\n\n3. **Null Handling**: Consider NULL values in expressions and joins\n\n4. **Performance**:\n   - Use pre-filters to reduce data volume early\n   - Static joins (`streaming: false`) are faster than streaming joins\n   - Temporary fields are cheaper than persisted fields\n\n5. **Schema Evolution**:\n   - Use `preserve: true` for unreferencedColumns to handle future schema changes\n     {{JSON_EXTRACT_SCHEMA_EVOLUTION_BULLET}}\n\n6. **Naming Conventions**:\n   - Use snake_case for field names\n   - Use descriptive names (not abbreviations)\n     {{JSON_EXTRACT_NAMING_BULLET}}\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Always start with schema discovery\n\nBefore configuring transformations, understand the bronze data:\n\n- What columns exist and their types\n  {{JSON_EXTRACT_SCHEMA_DISCOVERY_BULLET}}\n- What values look like (sample data)\n\n### Validate before applying\n\nBefore updating the datasource spec:\n\n- Validate field specs for syntax errors\n- Preview the transformation result\n- Confirm with user before making changes\n\n### Confirm with user\n\nWhen proposing configurations:\n\n- Explain what the change will do\n- Show expected impact with examples\n- Ask for confirmation before applying\n\n### Preview results\n\nAfter configuration changes:\n\n- A new preview will be automatically triggerred. The preview result may takes secs to mins to load ( with a different previewId )\n- Offer to retrieve preview result for the silver table\n- Verify the transformation produces expected output\n\n## Common Mistakes to Avoid\n\n### ❌ Referencing non-existent columns\n\n**Problem:** Field spec references `user_name` but bronze column is `userName`.\n\n**Impact:** Transformation fails with schema error.\n\n**Solution:** Always analyze bronze schema first to verify column names exist.\n\n### ❌ Using modifyTables for new tables\n\n**Problem:** Using `modifyTables` when the table doesn't exist in the preset.\n\n**Impact:** Configuration fails because the table can't be found.\n\n**Solution:** Use `addTables` to create new tables, `modifyTables` only for existing preset tables.\n\n### ❌ Unbalanced quotes or parentheses in expressions\n\n**Problem:** SQL expression has mismatched quotes or parentheses.\n\n**Impact:** Transformation fails with syntax error.\n\n**Solution:** Validate expressions before applying. Count opening/closing pairs.\n\n### ❌ Using == instead of = in SQL\n\n**Problem:** Writing `status == 'active'` instead of `status = 'active'`.\n\n**Impact:** SQL syntax error.\n\n**Solution:** SQL uses `=` for equality, not `==`.\n\n### ❌ Forgetting to add join tables to bronzeTables\n\n**Problem:** Referencing `emp_dir.department` without adding the join table to bronzeTables.\n\n**Impact:** Column reference fails because table isn't available.\n\n**Solution:** Always add external tables to `silver.bronzeTables` before referencing their columns.\n"}}]);
